Stop a resize from pulling scrollback back into view.

Splitting a pane narrows it. With the default, a pane that had just been
cleared would get its old lines back from scrollback above the prompt.

diff --git a/src/terminal/Terminal.zig b/src/terminal/Terminal.zig
index 75046ff..a5e9ed4 100644
--- a/src/terminal/Terminal.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/Terminal.zig
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ flags: packed struct {
     /// buffer without scrollback (e.g. Windows ConPTY) so that we stay in
     /// sync with it. See PageList.Resize for details. This is configuration
     /// rather than terminal state so it is preserved across a full reset.
-    resize_pull_scrollback: bool = true,
+    resize_pull_scrollback: bool = false,
 
     /// True if the terminal is in a password entry mode. This is set
     /// to true based on termios state. This is set
